<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan overnight rates end up on funds shortage.</title>
<headline>Pakistan overnight rates end up on funds shortage.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan overnight rates closed at 17 percent on Friday, up from the previous day's 11 percent close, due to a shortage of funds, dealers said.</p>
<p>Early overnight trades were struck at 9.00 percent but closed at 17 percent, a dealer at KASB &amp; Co Ltd said. In between, rates fell as low as 4.50 percent, he said.</p>
<p>Banks squared off their positions between 12 and 14 percent, the dealer said.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
